<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1612–1646</span> · Also known as Odoardo I Farnese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odoardo Farnese was duke of Parma and Piacenza from 1622. Seeking military glory, he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1635, bringing a devastating Spanish invasion of the Piacenza countryside until he made peace in 1637. He then fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-castro">First War of Castro</a> in 1641–1644 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-viii">Pope Urban VIII</a> and the Barberini family to keep his family's fief of Castro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odoardo-farnese-duke-of-parma.jpg" alt="Odoardo Farnese, Duke of Parma" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isacco Gioacchino Levi (1818-1908) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ritratto_di_Odoardo_Farnese.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
